{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A small, mostly-static content set favors running search fully in the browser — no round trip per query, after a one-time load.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Client-side pays once (model plus index download) and is free per query after that; server-side pays nothing upfront but costs a round trip on every query — match the choice to corpus size and change frequency.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Corpus size, update frequency, and whether the UI needs to be interactive immediately are the variables that actually decide this — and the two approaches can coexist in the same feature rather than being all-or-nothing.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
